e2ee3fda4a2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459285 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $9$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3,\\,9.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $15$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3,\\,5,\\,15.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $21$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3,\\,7,\\,21.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $9,$ $15,$ and $21$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $3.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. The expressions $9m,$ $15n,$ and $21n$ do not all share a variable factor.\n\nThus, the $\\text{GCF}$ of $9m,$ $15n,$ and $21n$ is $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
